# notify.sh / spend.sh config — copy to .notify.env and edit. Entirely optional:
# with no file at all, notifications work and the spend alert uses its default.
#
#   cp System_Config/.notify.env.example System_Config/.notify.env
#
# `cp` prints nothing on success — that silence IS success. The file is hidden
# (leading dot), so confirm with: ls -la System_Config/.notify.env
#
# .notify.env is git-ignored: it is machine-specific, not shared config.
# An explicitly exported variable beats this file for a single invocation, e.g.
#   NOTIFY_ENABLED=0 bash System_Config/notify.sh "quiet" "run"

# ── Delivery ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Notifications are local by default: macOS Notification Center via osascript, or
# notify-send where that exists — unconditional, no config needed. Webhook
# delivery (Slack, Google Chat) below is additive and strictly opt-in: leave both
# blank and nothing changes.
#
# Set to 0 to silence every notification from every script.
NOTIFY_ENABLED=1

# Optional Google Chat webhook — paste the "Space" webhook URL from
# Google Chat → Space settings → Apps & integrations → Webhooks. Quote it (the
# URL contains an unquoted `&`, which bash would otherwise treat as a control
# operator). Leave blank to skip Google Chat entirely.
# GCHAT_WEBHOOK_URL="https://chat.googleapis.com/v1/spaces/XXX/messages?key=...&token=..."

# Optional Slack incoming-webhook URL (Slack → Apps → Incoming Webhooks). Quote
# it. Leave blank to skip Slack entirely.
# SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL="https://hooks.slack.com/services/XXX/YYY/ZZZ"

# Heads up for local testing: setting either webhook above makes a THIRD-PARTY
# network call whenever notify.sh delivers — including from test.sh's stubbed
# notify.sh assertions, which assume no channel besides the (also stubbed) local
# notifier can succeed. Keep both blank on any machine that runs the test suite.

# ── Spend ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Alert once per day when the day's API spend crosses this figure (USD).
# Context: a single headless call from this workspace costs roughly $0.12 before
# doing any work (~50k tokens of fixed context load first), so a busy run of four
# tasks has a floor near $0.50. Inspect anytime with:
#   bash System_Config/spend.sh report
SPEND_ALERT_USD=10
